{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102220","id":2308006412,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6JkWIM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102220","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102220.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102220.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102220","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102220/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102220/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102220/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e77a011188f491f3e701f6741f23ac7462f82ffa","number":102220,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix a crash on iOS from Joypad initialization","user":{"login":"jkirsteins","id":135874,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTg3NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins","html_url":"https://github.com/jkirsteins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkirsteins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The way iOS initializes joypads right now will crash the app, if a gamepad is already connected before the game is started.\r\n\r\n`JoypadApple` starts listening for joypad notifications before the `Input` singleton is available. iOS will immediately send a notification about controllers already on and connected. This will lead to attempted use of the Input singleton before it's ready ([here is where the crash will happen](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/9ee1873ae1e09c217ac24a5800007f63cb895615/drivers/apple/joypad_apple.mm#L303)). \r\n\r\n`initialize_joypad()` on the other hand is called explicitly after the Input singleton becomes available ([here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/9ee1873ae1e09c217ac24a5800007f63cb895615/main/main.cpp#L2941)).\r\n\r\nFor context - the issue was introduced [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/cd17cb011075d110d1ea50f8a9c0573b22c3dc58#diff-f0ce1cbd4e741f31a64b71de9cc7633aacc3e1e75b16562b41df7d6142c3af45), and from the context it seems like it was probably an oversight.\r\n\r\n**Steps to reproduce**\r\n\r\n- Connect a hardware controller to an iOS device\r\n- Launch any Godot app","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097519,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1MTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:ios","name":"platform:ios","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","defaul